--- MESSAGE ---
A parenthesized sub-expression dissolves into its tree, and each renderer writes the minimal pair by its own target's fixity

A group holding one expression the parser reads is that expression's tree; the pair is not
information once the tree is associated, and a group the parser reads as a leaf keeps it. The
drake emitter writes back only the pairs drake's fixity needs, the Scala target only the pairs
Scala's precedence needs, where `++` ranks with `+` and every operator groups left, so the same
tree is parenthesized per target. TypeLoader's guard, the one grouped value in the corpus, lost
its redundant pair on both surfaces.

